>>
Rule 1 (threshold must be greater than or equal to the minimum value of the input tensor if value is set to min value)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_2 = min(v_1) then v_2 ≤ min(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (if threshold is positive, the value should also be positive, if specified)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_1 > 0 then v_2 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (threshold must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (value must be less than or equal to max if the threshold is set to the max)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_2 = max(v_1) then v_2 ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (if threshold is set to zero, the value should be less than or equal to zero)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_1 = 0 then v_2 ≤ 0
